<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- Entitlements for the hardened runtime on the `bithuman` CLI.

	     Each key below is here because a MEASURED failure required it, not
	     because it is commonly seen in signing recipes. The hardened runtime
	     is mandatory for notarization, and every entitlement listed here
	     RELAXES it, so the set is kept as small as the binary actually
	     tolerates. See scripts/sign-macos.sh. -->

	<!-- The CLI dlopen()s dylibs it did not ship: the expression-2 engine
	     that imx_fetch.rs can download at runtime into ~/.bithuman/lib, and
	     the native extensions in the managed brain venv under
	     ~/.cache/bithuman/brain-venv. Under the hardened runtime, library
	     validation refuses any dylib not signed by the same Team ID, which
	     would break both paths.

	     MEASURED, so this is not a cargo-culted key. A minimal dlopen host
	     signed with the same Developer ID and the hardened runtime, opening
	     the ad-hoc lible_core.dylib from the PyPI `bithuman` wheel:

	       no entitlements  -> dlopen FAILED, rc=1
	          "code signature ... not valid for use in process: mapping
	           process and mapped file (non-platform) have different Team IDs"
	       this entitlement -> DLOPEN_OK, rc=0

	     Remove this key and any dlopen of a dylib bitHuman did not sign
	     fails exactly that way. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
